

                   ADVENTURER-KINGS:  GAME 3, TURN 6

                                  FOR

                                 KWOTH







          Guido Pacifici
          
              
                              




  Quote of the Week:

  John II, King of Poland, after routing the Turks from Vienna in 1683 A.D.:
  "The immortal God... has blest us with so signal a victory as scarce the 
memory of man can equal.  Thanks be to Heaven, now the Half-Moon triumphs no 
longer over the Cross!"


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:

  In spring, Babba Sissoko (#0) informed Kwoth that our amicable 
relationship has been rendered worthless by Kwoth's despicable provocations.

  With the advent of the spring season, Kwoth set out to quench his thirst 
for glory.  Limerick was hit by a plague.  The Plague affected no armies in 
Limerick.  Kwoth moved into Limerick (#703) with his redoubtable army.
  The Daedalus Sea was hit by a plague.  The Plague affected no armies in 
the Daedalus Sea.  Gafsa was hit by a plague.  The Plague affected no armies 
in Gafsa.
  With the advent of the early summer season Kwoth announced a call for 
recruits in Limerick and was able to enlist the 15th Phalanx to fight for 
Kwoth.
  Khurum was hit by a plague.  The Plague affected no armies in Khurum.
  In late summer, Chaco was hit by a plague.  The Plague affected no armies 
in Chaco.  Kwoth tried a Tornado spell, but botched it.
  The Barents Sea was hit by a plague.  The Plague affected no armies in the 
Barents Sea.
  The hot days of summer mellowed into a colorful fall.  Circe (#8) cast a 
spell giving magical powers of oratory to Kwoth.
  Kwoth could not cast Part Sea on Ngara because it is a non-flooded land 
hex.  Instead, Kwoth tried to practice his Tactics, but the task seemed 
beyond his ability.  He conducted military exercises and the 15th Phalanx 
rose in quality.
  Magical tornadoes hit the defenders of Limerick.  Tornadoes sucked up the 
65th Legion in Limerick and destroyed them.  Tornadoes sucked up the 211th 
Camel Corps in Limerick and destroyed them.
  A conquering horde owing their allegiance to 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll (#1) invaded the province of Jerbilia, a 
Desert area owned by Kwoth.  Jerbilia was conquered and occupied by 
Uga-Buga Makumb's host.  Uga-Buga Makumb leads approximately 2 Bowmen, 4 
Dragons and 3 Trolls.

  A great host of warriors carried the banner of 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll into the Desert province of Gafsa, ruled 
by Kwoth.  Gafsa was overrun by Teleko (#72)'s host.  Teleko leads 
approximately 1 Dragons, 5 Eagles and 1 Trolls.
  In early winter, Kwoth cancelled his move to Ngara in order to fight for 
the province of Limerick.  So, Kwoth discovered nothing in his sagely 
experiments.

  Limerick was magically flooded.  Kwoth's forces fought in a battle in 
Chaco, but a foreign general commanded it.  The battle is in the General 
Intelligence Report.

  Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll (#1) ordered an invasion force into the 
adjacent Plain province of Limerick, owned by Kwoth.  Teleko (#72) was in 
command of the invading armies.  The defenders were led by Kwoth.  The 
armies were drawn up into lines of battle as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of Limerick (0703):

