  DEFENDING ARMY

  Teleko led his armies boldly into the battle.  Kwoth stood determinedly at 
the head of his thousands.  Circe (#8) led a host of loyal soldiers into the 
battle.
  Teleko (#72) strode forward and challenged Kwoth to personal combat.  
Kwoth answered the challenge to honorable combat.  Lifting his hands high in 
the air, Teleko cast a Spiritwrack spell, to make Kwoth quake and shiver 
with spiritual convulsions.
  Kwoth advanced to bow range.  Waving his hands, Teleko orchestrated 
supernatural forces of magic, casting a Holy Symbol spell.  A golden mist in 
the shape of a cross formed around Teleko.
  Kwoth charged into the melee.  Showing no fear, Kwoth moved closer and 
swang at Teleko and inflicted 3 damage points on him.  His spell was 
disrupted by the event.
  Kwoth swang at Teleko but his aim was slightly off the mark.  Teleko 
violently attacked Kwoth but Kwoth evaded the blow.  Kwoth deftly swang at 
Teleko and would have hit him if Teleko hadn't ducked just then.  Teleko 
forced back Kwoth with his spirited assault.  He then thrust at Kwoth with 
terrific strength but his sword whiffed harmlessly through the air.
  Teleko swang at Kwoth and missed badly.  Kwoth maneuvered for a good 
attacking vantage.  Then Kwoth swang at Teleko with all his might but his 
aim was just off the mark.  He thrust at his nemesis but Teleko dodged the 
sword.  Hoping to take advantage of a gap in Kwoth's defenses, Teleko thrust 
at Kwoth and scored on him, doing 2 points of damage.  Kwoth daringly swang 
at Teleko and would have hit him if Teleko hadn't ducked just then.  With 
surprising speed, Teleko thrust at Kwoth and damaged him, inflicting 5 
damage points.
  Teleko swang at Kwoth and scorched him with 2 damage points.  Kwoth 
feigned retreat, then whirled and thrust at Teleko and inflicted 3 damage 
points.  Teleko violently assailed Kwoth and inflicted 5 damage points on 
him.  Kwoth staggered, stunned by the force of the mortal blow.  Thus did 
Kwoth finally die, a defiant death by any standard.
  The forces commanded by Kwoth were disheartened by his death, yet still 
they moved ahead with some hope of victory.  Circe (#8) assumed command of 
the forces of the realm of Circe.  An unfavorable omen manifested itself, 
which of course dealt a severe blow to Teleko (#72)'s hopes.  Teleko's mount 
was shot and killed while Teleko was giving a speech.  On the other hand in 
this perilous slugging match, Teleko appeared to have the tactical edge.
  The Dragons commanded by Teleko were not impressed by his lack of 
leadership ability.  Using his arcane Spell of Oratory, Kwoth gave a rousing 
harangue to his troops, which bolstered their courage.  Circe (#8) started 
with a rousing harangue to her army, which bolstered their courage.  The 
Werefolk led by Circe were disgusted with her lack of leadership ability.
  On the right wing, the 319th Eagles faced the 261st Phalanx.  The 319th 
Eagles swooped down on the 261st Phalanx and attacked without mercy.  On 
this field, scouts of the 319th Eagles had been trapped before the battle.  
They were killed and their bodies catapulted over the 319th Eagles.  This 
goaded the 319th Eagles into a berserk attacking rage.
  But the battle was not yet over.  The 261st Phalanx's opponents were 
overjoyed when a beautiful golden eagle flew overhead, a wonderful omen.  
But their joy turned to despair when a boorish soldier killed the bird (a 
SURE sign of doom!)  The 319th Eagles fought the 261st Phalanx and battled 
them tooth and nail, neither side willing to give ground.
  Within the interior lines, the 322nd Eagles faced the 15th Phalanx.  The 
322nd Eagles swooped down on the 15th Phalanx and attacked without mercy.  
In this match, the men of the 322nd Eagles ran into some unpredictable 
footing and were afflicted with great disruption.  The 322nd Eagles fought 
the 15th Phalanx and could not hold their ground against their savage foe.
  In the interior lines, the Veteran 323rd Trolls were arrayed against the 
Crack 234th Legion.  In this area, many men of the 323rd Trolls were 
suffering from hangovers, weakening their fighting strength significantly.  
The 323rd Trolls battled the 234th Legion and could not quite hold their 
ground against their savage opponent.
  Within the interior lines, the 326th Dragons faced the 235th Legion.  The 
326th Dragons fought with the 235th Legion and could not stand their ground 
and executed an orderly retreat.
  Within the interior front, the 321st Eagles were arrayed against the 
Veteran 67th Legion.  The 321st Eagles swooped down on the 67th Legion and 
attacked them.  Here, some of the 67th Legion had been drawn off by the need 
to take a small but centrally situated castle, so they were far below their 
usual strength.  Still, the 321st Eagles battled with the 67th Legion and 
could not quite hold their ground against their determined foe.
  On the left wing, the 320th Eagles faced the 26th Were-Beasts, who were 
stiffened by a tough outfit of freedom fighters of the Mercenaries Guild, 
who led them into a fanatical fervor by example of their fearless elan.  The 
320th Eagles swooped down on the 26th Were-Beasts and attacked without 
mercy.  Here, the musicians of the 26th Were-Beasts bravely volunteered to 
march in the van, and all the soldiers were stirred by their spirited 
singing.  The 320th Eagles battled the 26th Were-Beasts and battled them to 
a standstill.
  Circe's great horde overwhelmed the army of Uga-Buga Makumb (#1) and took 
the field, scattering their enemies.
  Though Circe (#8)'s forces were triumphant, Teleko (#72) rallied his men 
and decided to contest Limerick.
  Thus endeth the adventures of Kwoth for this year.


  Kwoth treated with his ally Bradipo I (#2).  Kwoth treated with his ally 
Hokuto (#4).  Kwoth treated with his ally Prometeo (#5).  Kwoth treated with 
his ally Kahn (#6).  Kwoth treated with his ally Giovanna d'Arco (#7).  
Kwoth treated with his ally Circe (#8).  Kwoth treated with his ally 
Agesilao (#9).
  Your Majesty, I have news to report of wanderers in our kingdom:  
  The 213th Chariots has wandered into Chirfa from Silvermist.


  Here is the financial report for Kwoth's kingdom: this turn, the Kingdom 
collected 14 gold in revenue.  2 gold was expended to finance our leaders.  
The 115th Fleet trained well and improved in quality.  13 gold was expended 
to maintain our armies.  Kwoth was left with 37 gold in the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Samantha
To: Kwoth

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Frigid winter gave way to spring, and I made ready to carry out my urgent 
orders.  I rode into the Daedalus Sea.
  With the advent of the early summer season I announced a plea for recruits 
in the Daedalus Sea and was able to form the 115th Fleet to fight for me.
  In late summer, I sailed into the Barents Sea (#802) with my formidable 
forces.
  The hot days of summer mellowed into a colorful fall.  I sailed my command 
into Khurum (#903).
  While speaking to some friendly locals, I heard a rumor about a Maze in 
the Buccaneer Sea (#806), occupied by the Minotaur.  They say that 
the Minotaur actually owns the Periodic Table of Elements.
  With the coming of the early winter season I discovered nothing in my 
sagely researches.

  Thy humble servant,   Samantha


From: Clarambald
To: Kwoth

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I moved into Tebessa.  While adventuring, I saw no wandering 
monsters.
  The wet spring was followed by a sultry early summer.  I was magically 
killed by a dark Necromantic spell!  And so it was that I met my unseemly 
end.

  Thy humble servant,   Clarambald


