GENERAL INTELLIGENCE REPORT

Kingdom of Uga-Buga Makumb (#1):
  In spring, Tebessa was hit by a plague.
  In late summer, Kabompo was hit by a plague.
  In early winter, Uga-Buga Makumb (#1) flew into Chaco.  Uga-Buga Makumb 
commanded the attacking armies.  The defenders were led by Hokuto (#4).
  In early winter, the 321st Eagles and the 326th Dragons trained well and 
improved in quality.
  In fall, Teleko (#72) flew over to Gafsa.
  In early winter, Teleko rode his flying armies into Limerick.
  In fall, tornadoes sucked up the 20th Legion in Limerick and destroyed 
them.  Tornadoes sucked up the 21st Light Cavalry in Limerick and destroyed 
them.  Tornadoes sucked up the 22nd Legion in Limerick and destroyed them.  
Tornadoes sucked up the 246th Camel Corps in Limerick and destroyed them.  
Tornadoes sucked up the 343rd Bowmen in Limerick and destroyed them.
