  DEFENDING ARMY

  Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll (#1) stood determinedly at the head of 
his thousands.  Hokuto (#4) marched with his loyal troops, eyes set in grim 
determination.
  Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll (#1) strode forward and challenged 
Hokuto (#4) to honorable combat.  Hokuto bravely answered the invitation to 
personal combat.  Thus did Hokuto die, a defiant death by any standard.  The 
forces commanded by Hokuto were disheartened by his death, yet still they 
moved ahead with some hope of victory.  Uga-Buga Makumb (#1)'s fortunes took 
a turn for the better when his scouts located a high granite outcropping, 
which was well suited as an artillery site.  Further, his clever tactical 
maneuvers gave his forces an undeniable advantage.

  Out on the right outside wing, the Veteran 316th Bowmen were arrayed 
against the Veteran 282nd Legion.  The 315th Dragons swooped down on the 
267th Chariots and attacked without mercy.  The poor horses of the 267th 
Chariots were spooked by the howls of the terrible Beasts they beheld.  The 
316th Bowmen battled with the 282nd Legion and steadily advanced against 
them.
  In the interior front, the 293rd Dragons were descended upon by the Circle 
of Wraiths, who goaded them into mindless fanatical battle-lust with their 
maniacal laughter.  They faced the Crack 70th Chariots.  The 293rd Dragons 
swooped down on the 70th Chariots and attacked them.  The horses of the 70th 
Chariots were frightened by the fearsome Beasts they beheld.  The horses of 
the 284th Chariots were frightened by the Beasts they were faced with.  In 
this match, the supreme commander condescended to personally ride with the 
troops of the 293rd Dragons in the front lines, inspiring them to a 
surpassing performance.  The 293rd Dragons fought with the 70th Chariots and 
advanced at will.
  Within the interior lines, the 317th Trolls were arrayed against the 
Veteran 71st Legion.  Here, the 71st Legion carelessly stumbled into a nest 
of booby traps and lost some of their best battle-hardened troops.  The 
317th Trolls fought with the 71st Legion and determinedly plowed into their 
opponents.
  In the interior lines, the Veteran 314th Dragons faced the Veteran 283rd 
Legion.  The 314th Dragons swooped down on the 283rd Legion and attacked 
without mercy.  On this battleground, the soldiers of the 314th Dragons 
noticed the presence of an encampment of trollops behind their opponents' 
lines, so they lustily concentrated their efforts to smash through.  The 
outcome seemed bleak for the brave fighters of the 283rd Legion.
  But would victory yet be snatched from the jaws of defeat?  A fantastic 
omen heartened the 283rd Legion.  A flight of silver dragons floated over, 
and their magic mists settled upon the 283rd Legion.  In spite of the 283rd 
Legion's good fortune, the 314th Dragons battled with the 283rd Legion and 
moved ahead slowly, contested for every foot of their advance.
  Out on the left outside wing, the 318th Trolls were arrayed against the 
233rd Chariots.  In this sector, the 233rd Chariots were fearful of defeat.  
But then the 233rd Chariots's regimental high priest picked up his pike and 
joined the battle, and the 233rd Chariots rallied fiercely.  In spite of the 
233rd Chariots's good luck, the 318th Trolls battled the 233rd Chariots and 
steadily advanced against them.
  Uga-Buga Makumb's great horde overwhelmed the army of Kwoth and took the 
field, scattering their enemies.  The 316th Bowmen demolished the 282nd 
Legion.  The 293rd Dragons slew the 70th Chariots almost to a man.  The 
314th Dragons scattered the 283rd Legion in all directions.  The 315th 
Dragons destroyed the 267th Chariots.  The 293rd Dragons gave chase and 
annihilated the 83rd Camel Corps.  The 314th Dragons overtook the enemy and 
demolished the 155th Chariots.  The 315th Dragons chased after the enemy and 
slew the 284th Chariots almost to a man.  Uga-Buga Makumb's campaign 
effected the conquest of Chaco.  The acting commander withdrew to Balmwood, 
beaten but not discouraged.
  In spring, Ningarl (#13) marched on Starhaven (#701) with his forces.
  In early summer, Lexington cast a Bless spell.

Kingdom of Circe (#8):
  In spring, Circe (#8) moved into Chirfa (#603) with her army.
  In early summer, Circe cast a spell giving magical powers of oratory to 
Circe.
  In late summer, Circe moved into Limerick (#703) with her redoubtable 
army.
  In early winter, Circe treated with her ally Bradipo I (#2).  Circe (#8) 
treated with her ally Hokuto (#4).  Circe (#8) treated with her ally 
Prometeo (#5).  Circe (#8) treated with her ally Kahn (#6).  Circe (#8) 
treated with her ally Giovanna d'Arco (#7).  Circe (#8) treated with her 
ally Agesilao (#9).


